Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 21:54:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 140/162] feat: clouds look the same through every camera -
 sky-ray unclamp and edge fade are engine behaviour (ReCS)

User policy (2026-09-09): the cloud layer must not render differently through the Default
editor camera and through CineCam / a cinematic camera. So the sky-ray rule from ed573597 is
no longer gated on the scene-referred path: every sky ray marches to the cloud shell and the
max viewable distance, real geometry still clamps. Same class of change as the
e_VolumetricFog default - a ReCS engine behaviour, stated as such.

Also added, in both visible march techniques: an edge fade for SKY rays. Whatever ends the
march (max viewable distance, max ray-march length) does so with a hard boundary in
elevation; the pass's colour and (1 - transmittance) now fade out over the last 4 km of
marched segment, for the main colour and the min-depth twin, so the cloud region's sky blends
into the plain sky below instead of stepping. Rays that stop on geometry keep their full
contribution - the cloud in front of a mountain is real.

The cbuffer lane skyRayUnclamped is now informational (overlay: "sky rays past ZF + edge fade
yes (ReCS, all cameras)"); the shader applies the rule without reading it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
